 "badge": {
  "id": "long-column",
  "name": "The Long Column"
 },
 "briefing": {
  "situation": "3 November 1944. You and a wingman are airborne west of the central ridge after a fruitless search for shipping off Ormoc. A Japanese column is moving up the valley road: tanks, trucks and a staff car with two guns and light flak along the way. Stop or destroy at least ten of its fifteen powered vehicles, two of them tanks, then land at Tacloban.",
  "loadout": "both"
 },
 "history": {
  "text": "On 3 November 1944 fifteen P-38s, after a shipping search off Ormoc, found a column about ten miles long of trucks, artillery and tanks on the Ormoc-Valencia road and attacked it. This mission is inspired by that action rather than a reconstruction of it, with the force compressed: the game shows a representative column of nineteen gameplay entities, not a literal ten-mile traffic file, and its vehicle types and the field-gun mix are representative.",
  "sources": [
   "U.S. Army, Leyte: The Return to the Philippines, ch. VI: https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/USA/USA-P-Return/USA-P-Return-6.html",
   "Army Air Forces, The Pacific: Guadalcanal to Saipan, ch. XII: https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/AAF/V/AAF-V-12.html"
  ]
 }
}